.TH CLAUDRON 1 "2026-09-02" "claudron" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claudron \- align Claude usage windows with your working day
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claudron
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Claude usage window opens on the first message sent while no window is open,
and lasts five hours. A message sent while a window is already open changes
nothing. The times you send that first message therefore decide when your
limits reset.
.PP
.B claudron
sends that message at times you choose, reads your real usage from Claude
Code's local transcripts, and tells you when to stay quiet so an accidental
message does not open a window early and push every later reset out of
alignment.
.PP
Because a day is 24 hours and a window is five, a schedule that repeats daily
holds at most four anchors covering 20 of 24 hours. At least four hours are
idle; the only choice is where they land.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use an alternate configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create a configuration file, optionally from a named preset.
.TP
.B suggest
Propose anchor times that fit your day. Describe when you sleep
.RB ( \-\-sleep ),
when you are away
.RB ( \-\-idle ),
when you really work
.RB ( \-\-busy ),
and the times you need
.RB ( \-\-start\-at ", " \-\-free\-at );
every legal arrangement is searched and ranked by where the unavoidable idle
hours land.
.B \-\-apply
writes the chosen option into the configuration file.
.TP
.B status
The window that is open now, the tokens spent in it, whether it matches your
plan, and the next anchor.
.B \-\-short
prints one line, suitable for a status bar.
.TP
.B plan
Simulate a day: a 24\-hour timeline, the anchors, the idle gaps, and any anchor
that would open nothing.
.B \-\-live
seeds the simulation with the window that is actually open.
.TP
.B usage
Real token usage per window, read from local transcripts.
.TP
.B fire
Send an anchor message now.
.B \-\-dry\-run
prints the exact command without sending anything.
.B \-\-scheduled
fires only when an anchor is due, and is what the timer unit runs.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the supervisor in the foreground: fire anchors, catch up after suspend, and
warn when a window opens inside an idle gap.
.TP
.B install
Install a systemd user timer, a systemd service, a launchd agent, or print cron
lines.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the installed schedule.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the environment and the schedule.
.TP
.B completion
Print a shell completion script for bash, zsh or fish.
.TP
.B config
Inspect configuration:
.BR path ", " show ", or " presets .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The schedule contains an error, or no schedule satisfies the given constraints.
.TP
.B 2
The configuration is missing or invalid.
.TP
.B 3
Something in the environment is missing, such as the \fBclaude\fR CLI.
.TP
.B 4
Firing an anchor failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claudron/config.toml
Configuration. Override the directory with \fBCLAUDRON_CONFIG_DIR\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/claudron/
State, the transcript cache, and the log. Override with \fBCLAUDRON_STATE_DIR\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/
Claude Code's transcripts, read for usage. Only the timestamp, message type,
model id and token counts are parsed; message content is never read.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDRON_CONFIG_DIR
Override the configuration directory.
.TP
.B CLAUDRON_STATE_DIR
Override the state directory.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour output.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
When set to \fBtruecolor\fR or \fB24bit\fR, banners use the pixel logo.
.SH NOTES
claudron cannot tell you how much of your rate limit is left. Anthropic does
not publish that figure to the local machine, so claudron reports token counts
and compares them against your own busiest window instead of guessing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Work out a schedule, apply it, and run it unattended:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
claudron suggest \-\-start\-at 12:00 \-\-sleep 23:00\-05:00 \-\-apply 1
claudron plan
claudron doctor
claudron install
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage and full documentation:
.UR https://locngoduc.github.io/claudron/
.UE
